## Summary

Fixed `f2-expiry-skipped-when-auth-unresolvable`: in `poll_once` (`crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/batch_review.rs`), the bounded-wait deadline is now checked **before** any `batch_auth`/client/credential resolution, so a row whose repository batch policy becomes unresolvable (e.g. after `batch-review disable`) still expires and falls back to interactive review within its bound instead of being orphaned in `submitted` forever. Made `poll_once` `pub` for testability, and added `poller_expires_a_row_whose_repository_policy_is_no_longer_configured` in `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/tests/batch_review.rs`, which submits a row, disables its repository's batch policy, forces the deadline into the past, drives one poll pass, and asserts the row transitions to `expired_fallback` with reason `max_batch_wait_exceeded`.

All required verification passed: `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy` (workspace lints), and the full test suite across `familiar-ai-core`, `familiar-ai-review`, `familiar-ai-agent`, `familiar-ai-storage`, and `familiar-ai-daemon` (all green, including the identity-gate test after correcting placeholder paths to `familiar-ai.sock`/`familiar-ai.pid`). No commits were made.
